{
  "version": 1,
  "decision": "unchanged",
  "scope": "Introduce an offline data-license registry, SPDX identifier checks, generated per-package source notices, and validation before local preparation/CI/npm publishing. No source-data rows, SQL, indexes, runtime/API fan-out, D1 import tools or Worker bindings change. Derived package edits only add notices and correct package license summaries.",
  "beforeAfter": "Incremental account-wide D1 reads/writes remain 0/0 rows. The validator reads local files; its optional SQLite operation reads only local sqlite_schema in mode=ro. All 38 ordered download rows and data hashes match; moji.db SHA-256 remains c8cd43031d6a48bde6b131f0fd0fb778301627846c4b65ff038937884c21ea6b. Comment/package/prepare edits may invalidate local fingerprints and rebuild locally, without changing input values or deployed request work.",
  "accountBudget": "Offline checks, local tests, four real Yarn packs and npm release validation consume zero D1 rows account-wide, including retries. The release workflow performs no remote D1 query/import or Worker deployment. No current account usage is sampled because this operation has a zero D1 upper bound; traffic reserves are untouched, and no subsequent remote operation is authorized.",
  "validation": "22 validator tests and five existing DB fingerprint tests pass. Verified all 38 cached downloads, two cached npm archives/datasets and the tracked build-only input. A read-only local schema check resolves every affected table/view pattern. All four real Yarn archives preserve required notice/manifest bytes and omit build-only metadata. Workflow YAML and shell syntax pass; source rows and DB bytes match the baseline.",
  "rolloutAndStop": "Release metadata through ordinary patch npm releases. Stop on unknown identifiers, undefined LicenseRef terms, stale source/notice checksums, generated-file drift, missing archive notices, stale quota fingerprints, or unexpected data/runtime changes. Fix notice errors in a later package release; no D1 migration/rollback is needed. This record grants no permission or quota for a remote import/deployment.",
